  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor.header": "Experimental Reactor: Formation and Safe Control",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor.text_1": "A fixed 5x5x5 reactor starts with its casing and valid side interfaces.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor.text_2": "In this temporary teaching cutaway, each refueling port caps three fuel-rod blocks; the control-rod drive caps an air column, with no placeable control-rod block. After inspection, restore the walls and seal the roof with refueling ports, the drive, and casing before formation.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor.text_3": "The single instrument port owns reactor state. A Create wrench requests one server-side formation diagnostic: exactly one instrument port, at least one valid cold port and hot port, plus the casing and column layout; it does not change reactor state.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor.text_4": "With Create engineer goggles, the instrument shows formed size, fuel and control-rod columns, cold and hot port counts, count of coolant-space blocks, per-block capacity, and one layout-derived shared capacity in mB—not current stock. Runtime heat and per-column data come later.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor.text_5": "A newly formed reactor sets every movable control rod's target and actual depth to fully inserted. The drive caps an empty column; no fake control-rod blocks are placed below it.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor.text_6": "Every player may adjust each drive with its own server-validated Create-style slider. The client previews continuously; the server commits the target, and redstone does not adjust the drive.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor.text_7": "Multiple cold ports feed one shared coolant ledger. Each physical port has its configured per-tick quota; adding a port increases input throughput without creating another inventory or capacity.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor.text_8": "Multiple hot ports draw hot coolant from the same layout-derived shared capacity. Conversion changes coolant state without changing volume; output throughput and backpressure still control how long cooling can continue.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor.text_9": "Holding a high redstone signal at the instrument port requests SCRAM, saves the earlier targets, and commands every still-movable control rod fully inserted. This request does not promise success for every layout or a jammed rod.",
  "create_nuclear_industry.ponder.experimental_reactor.text_10": "Removing the signal clears SCRAM and restores the saved pre-SCRAM target depths. Fuel and residual heat are never deleted by the redstone request.",
